{"id":"f11t2","name":"Payment Retries in EUR","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["spark","attempts_df","rates_df"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>When a card payment fails, our payment service retries it automatically, up to several times. Every try is logged in <code>attempts_df</code> with the columns <code>payment_id</code>, <code>merchant</code>, <code>attempt_at</code> (timestamp), <code>status</code>, <code>amount</code> (double) and <code>currency</code>. The merchant team wants to know how well retries work and how much money they bring, in euros.</p>\n<p>A payment is <b>successful</b> as soon as one of its tries has the status <code>succeeded</code>; whatever is logged after its first success (duplicate notifications from the bank, for example) must be ignored. A payment that never succeeded is <b>failed</b> if its last try is <code>failed</code>; a payment whose last try is anything else is still in progress and does not count at all. The amount and the currency of a payment are those of its <b>first</b> try, because later tries are sometimes logged with a rounded amount.</p>\n<p><code>rates_df</code> has the columns <code>currency</code>, <code>day</code> (date) and <code>eur_rate</code> (double: 1 unit of the currency is worth <code>eur_rate</code> euros). Rates are not published every day: a successful payment is converted with the most recent rate of its currency published on or before the day of its first success. Euros are never in <code>rates_df</code> and have a rate of 1. A successful payment with no known rate is still counted as successful, but brings no euros.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return one row per merchant with at least one successful or failed payment, with the columns <code>merchant</code>, <code>succeeded</code> (long), <code>failed</code> (long), <code>avg_tries</code> (double: average number of tries up to and including the first success, over successful payments, rounded to 2 decimals, <code>null</code> if none) and <code>revenue_eur</code> (double, sum of the converted amounts of the successful payments, rounded to 2 decimals, <code>0.0</code> if none). Sort by <code>merchant</code>. Statuses may be written in any case.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p><code>attempts_df</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>payment_id</th><th>merchant</th><th>attempt_at</th><th>status</th><th>amount</th><th>currency</th></tr><tr><td>p1</td><td>shopA</td><td>2026-03-01 10:00:00</td><td>failed</td><td>100.0</td><td>MAD</td></tr><tr><td>p1</td><td>shopA</td><td>2026-03-01 10:05:00</td><td>Succeeded</td><td>100.0</td><td>MAD</td></tr><tr><td>p1</td><td>shopA</td><td>2026-03-01 10:06:00</td><td>failed</td><td>100.0</td><td>MAD</td></tr><tr><td>p2</td><td>shopA</td><td>2026-03-02 09:00:00</td><td>succeeded</td><td>20.0</td><td>EUR</td></tr><tr><td>p3</td><td>shopA</td><td>2026-03-02 11:00:00</td><td>failed</td><td>5.0</td><td>USD</td></tr><tr><td>p3</td><td>shopA</td><td>2026-03-02 11:10:00</td><td>FAILED</td><td>5.0</td><td>USD</td></tr><tr><td>p4</td><td>shopB</td><td>2026-03-03 08:00:00</td><td>failed</td><td>49.99</td><td>USD</td></tr><tr><td>p4</td><td>shopB</td><td>2026-03-03 08:30:00</td><td>pending</td><td>50.0</td><td>USD</td></tr><tr><td>p5</td><td>shopB</td><td>2026-03-03 12:00:00</td><td>failed</td><td>30.4</td><td>USD</td></tr><tr><td>p5</td><td>shopB</td><td>2026-03-04 12:00:00</td><td>succeeded</td><td>30.0</td><td>USD</td></tr><tr><td>p6</td><td>shopB</td><td>2026-03-04 13:00:00</td><td>succeeded</td><td>7.0</td><td>XOF</td></tr></table></div><p><code>rates_df</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>currency</th><th>day</th><th>eur_rate</th></tr><tr><td>MAD</td><td>2026-02-27</td><td>0.092</td></tr><tr><td>MAD</td><td>2026-03-02</td><td>0.093</td></tr><tr><td>USD</td><td>2026-03-01</td><td>0.92</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>merchant</th><th>succeeded</th><th>failed</th><th>avg_tries</th><th>revenue_eur</th></tr><tr><td>shopA</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>1.5</td><td>29.2</td></tr><tr><td>shopB</td><td>2</td><td>0</td><td>1.5</td><td>27.97</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB<br><b>[input]</b> DataFrame attempts_df<br><b>[input]</b> DataFrame rates_df<br><b>[output]</b> DataFrame with exactly the columns <code>merchant</code>, <code>succeeded</code>, <code>failed</code>, <code>avg_tries</code>, <code>revenue_eur</code>, in this order; rows in the order given by the statement</div>","starter":"from pyspark.sql import SparkSession, DataFrame, functions as F\nfrom pyspark.sql.window import Window\n\n\ndef solve(spark: SparkSession, attempts_df: DataFrame, rates_df: DataFrame) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return attempts_df\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["consigne longue","première réussite","taux de change as-of","plusieurs règles cachées"],"minutes":22,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>solution.py</code>.</li><li>Complète la fonction <code>solve(spark, attempts_df, rates_df)</code>. Garde son nom et ses paramètres : ce sont les tests qui l'appellent, avec leurs propres données. N'écris pas d'appel à la fonction toi-même.</li><li><code>spark</code> est une SparkSession déjà prête : ne crée pas la tienne.</li><li><code>attempts_df</code>, <code>rates_df</code> sont des DataFrames déjà chargés : ses colonnes sont celles de l'énoncé (onglet <b>Input</b> d'un test pour les voir).</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Ta fonction doit <b>renvoyer</b> le résultat avec <code>return</code>. Un <code>print</code> ou un <code>show()</code> ne compte pas : il sort seulement dans l'onglet <b>Console Output</b>.</li><li>Le DataFrame renvoyé doit avoir <b>exactement 5 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>merchant</code>, <code>succeeded</code>, <code>failed</code>, <code>avg_tries</code>, <code>revenue_eur</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Finis par un <code>select(...)</code> de ces colonnes.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>orderBy</code> à la fin).</li><li>Valeurs : les nombres sont comparés à 0,000001 près : arrondis seulement là où l'énoncé le demande, et au nombre de décimales demandé ; une case vide attendue s'écrit <code>null</code> : ce n'est ni <code>0</code> ni une chaîne vide.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Spark tourne dans ton Codespace : au premier RUN TESTS de la séance, attends qu'il soit prêt (1 à 2 minutes). Ensuite chaque lancement prend quelques secondes.</li><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 6 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"attempts_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"payment_id string, merchant string, attempt_at timestamp, status string, amount double, currency string","rows":[["p1","shopA","2026-03-01 10:00:00","failed",100.0,"MAD"],["p1","shopA","2026-03-01 10:05:00","Succeeded",100.0,"MAD"],["p1","shopA","2026-03-01 10:06:00","failed",100.0,"MAD"],["p2","shopA","2026-03-02 09:00:00","succeeded",20.0,"EUR"],["p3","shopA","2026-03-02 11:00:00","failed",5.0,"USD"],["p3","shopA","2026-03-02 11:10:00","FAILED",5.0,"USD"],["p4","shopB","2026-03-03 08:00:00","failed",49.99,"USD"],["p4","shopB","2026-03-03 08:30:00","pending",50.0,"USD"],["p5","shopB","2026-03-03 12:00:00","failed",30.4,"USD"],["p5","shopB","2026-03-04 12:00:00","succeeded",30.0,"USD"],["p6","shopB","2026-03-04 13:00:00","succeeded",7.0,"XOF"]]}},"rates_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"currency string, day date, eur_rate double","rows":[["MAD","2026-02-27",0.092],["MAD","2026-03-02",0.093],["USD","2026-03-01",0.92]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["merchant","succeeded","failed","avg_tries","revenue_eur"],"rows":[["shopA",2,1,1.5,29.2],["shopB",2,0,1.5,27.97]]}},{"input":{"attempts_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"payment_id string, merchant string, attempt_at timestamp, status string, amount double, currency string","rows":[["q","m","2026-03-05 10:00:00","pending",10.0,"USD"]]}},"rates_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"currency string, day date, eur_rate double","rows":[["USD","2026-03-01",0.9]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["merchant","succeeded","failed","avg_tries","revenue_eur"],"rows":[]}}],"hidden_n":6,"hidden":"","solution":""}